    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "For either x<0 or x>0, 2x² is positive, so f(x,y)=2x²y has the sign of y. Thus both top entries are positive and both bottom entries negative. Current option 4 agrees with this question's captured final sign table. The zero set is x=0 or y=0; the source's wording lists the two axes.",
